{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T05:13:40.146Z","ordinal":105908,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20bb2-48c0-7db0-bfc5-137d3a66f0eb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e0f0b73b-37f1-4f57-9614-98e65f131b2f","process_id":"4012","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '170,235p' eval/dataset.test.mjs; rg -n 'eval.dataset|eval dataset|Eval dataset' docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md eval/README.md docs/DEVELOPMENT.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '170,235p' eval/dataset.test.mjs","name":"dataset.test.mjs","path":"eval/dataset.test.mjs"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'eval.dataset|eval dataset|Eval dataset' docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md eval/README.md docs/DEVELOPMENT.md","query":"eval.dataset|eval dataset|Eval dataset","path":"CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(row.dir, \"oversized.bin\"), \"x\");\n    assert.throws(() => integrity.assertTaskSnapshotDigest({\n      dir: row.dir,\n      treeSha256: row.treeSha256,\n      id: row.id,\n      versionedDataset: true,\n    }), /digest mismatch|exceeds/);\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(temp, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"importable runner API passes only evaluator config and keeps credentials private\", async () => {\n  const api = await import(\"./runner_api.mjs\");\n  assert.equal(typeof api.runVersionedEvaluation, \"function\", \"runner API must export versioned evaluation\");\n  const temp = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-runner-api-test-\"));\n  try {\n    const executable = path.join(temp, \"nexus\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(executable, \"#!/bin/sh\\nexit 0\\n\", { mode: 0o700 });\n    const outputDir = path.join(temp, \"output\");\n    let observed;\n    const result = await api.runVersionedEvaluation({\n      config: { apiKey: \"synthetic-test-key\", steps: 3 },\n      nexusExecutable: executable,\n      dataset: datasetRoot,\n      outputDir,\n      split: \"regression\",\n      runs: 2,\n      cwd: temp,\n    }, {\n      run: ({ configPath, ...options }) => {\n        const config = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(configPath, \"utf8\"));\n        observed = {\n          configPath, config, configMode: fs.statSync(configPath).mode & 0o777,\n          credential: fs.readFileSync(config.apiKey.file, \"utf8\"),\n          credentialMode: fs.statSync(config.apiKey.file).mode & 0o777,\n          options,\n        };\n        fs.mkdirSync(options.outputDir, { mode: 0o700 });\n        fs.writeFileSync(path.join(options.outputDir, \"results.jsonl\"), \"{}\\n\");\n      },\n      score: () => ({ taskCount: 1, passRate: 1 }),\n    });\n\n    assert.equal(observed.config.agent, \"nexus\");\n    assert.equal(observed.config.nexusExecutable, executable);\n    assert.deepEqual(observed.config.apiKey, { file: path.join(path.dirname(observed.configPath), \"api-key.env\"), var: \"NEXUS_EVAL_API_KEY\" });\n    assert.equal(observed.configMode, 0o600);\n    assert.equal(observed.credentialMode, 0o600);\n    assert.equal(observed.credential, \"NEXUS_EVAL_API_KEY=REDACTED;\n    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(observed.options.dataset), true);\n    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(observed.configPath), false, \"private runner configuration is removed after completion\");\n    assert.deepEqual(result.score, { taskCount: 1, passRate: 1 });\n    assert.equal(JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(result.scoreFile, \"utf8\")).passRate, 1);\n    assert.equal(fs.statSync(result.scoreFile).mode & 0o777, 0o600);\n    await assert.rejects(api.runVersionedEvaluation({\n      config: {}, nexusExecutable: executable, dataset: datasetRoot, outputDir,\n    }), /output directory must not already exist/);\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(temp, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"dataset loader accepts and decouples code evaluator declarations\", async () => {\n  const loadDataset = requiredLoader();\n  const temp = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-evaluator-decouple-\"));\neval/README.md:78:The committed `eval/datasets/core-v1/` is the first migrated population: one regression self-test and six benchmark\neval/README.md:79:tasks. It can be run through the installed CLI with `nexus eval --dataset eval/datasets/core-v1 --split benchmark`. Held-out qualification corpora remain under their separately approved custody process and are not copied into\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:96:| `node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/eval_dataset.test.ts` (rebased branch; evaluator helper restored to committed mode 0644) | 3 passed, 0 failed | The test initially failed because the shared checkout materialized `eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs` as group-writable (0664), which the evaluator correctly rejects. Correcting only the local file mode to the committed non-writable mode made the provider-stimulus and hidden-validator checks pass; no source or assertion was changed. |\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:99:| `make test` (corrected detached snapshot `2502ae1b`, based on `a5faa878`, with `make build` outputs in the expected paths) | Failed overall, exit 2. Core 53/53, TUI 406/406, scope fixtures, and security lifecycle gates passed. The CLI shard reported 3 failures among 2,493 completed segments and timed out `compaction_continuity.test.ts`. | The run had the compiled CLI and Rust core at expected paths. Failure output includes `eval_dataset.test.ts` (“provider request contains the selected stimulus”); the shard also reported an `ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE` and further assertion failure(s), which were not fully recovered from the sharded output. This is not a clean full-suite qualification; the failures need triage. |\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:108:After rebasing onto PR #739, focused checks passed on the rebased source: context inventory 14/14, provider wire matrix 90/90, agent harness 90/90, slash router 39/39, knowledge controls 3/3, session durable fields 4/4, and persistence protection 27/27. The CLI build passed. On snapshot `48bb93f2` (based on `cebb31ac`, before PR #742), the full turn-semantics suite passed 37/37 and the focused long-step case passed 1/1 after the runtime binaries were placed where the CLI resolves them. After rebasing onto PR #742 at `a57c6c24`, exact-current-source checks passed on `b588d970`: CLI build, context inventory 14/14, knowledge controls 3/3, and provider wire matrix 90/90. At `03b62aaf`, `make build` passed, then `make test` was run with isolated CI-like workspace/runtime fixtures. Rust core passed 53/53, and scope fixtures/security gates passed; the aggregate command failed. Its aggregate test count was not available from the sharded runner output. The isolated `eval_dataset.test.ts` and standalone server-profile eval both fail closed before inference with `compiler exposure could not be checked; refusing qualification`; the gateway saw only the model-list probe, not a chat request. The version-probe test initially rejected the temporary `/tmp` runtime root; a retry used `/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime` and a private 128 MiB tmpfs with the required owner-only mount mode, but the host's bubblewrap could not access the workspace through its `/tmp` parent path. No protected fixture or guard was changed to bypass these checks. The D-04 behavior test exposed an obsolete assertion that expected model-originated `manage_knowledge` to persist durable memory. The test now asserts that this call is rejected and creates no knowledge file; `turn_verdict_evidence.test.ts` passes 26/26. After rebasing onto the latest `origin/release/v1.3.0` at `10942d41`, the focused checks before budget work passed: context inventory 14/14, knowledge controls 3/3, provider wire matrix 90/90, and turn verdict 26/26. The bounded-budget and prompt-provenance implementation passed `npm run build`, `context_inventory.test.ts` 16/16, knowledge controls 3/3, provider wire matrix 90/90, slash router 39/39, persistence protection 27/27, and skill injection 15/15 on exact snapshot `2502ae1b`. The corrected `make test` on snapshot `2502ae1b` passed core 53/53, TUI 406/406, scope fixtures and security gates, but failed overall in the CLI shard: 2,493 completed segments, 3 failures, and a timeout in `compaction_continuity.test.ts`. Focused reruns show the dataset failure came from the local shared-checkout mode of the trusted evaluator helper, and the compaction file completes when the watchdog allows its declared 900-second test timeout. Two of the three CLI failures remain unclassified because the shard output was truncated. The full suite has not been rerun after correcting those local conditions or after rebasing onto `cd755b3e`; repository-wide qualification remains pending.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":656396245}},"started_at_ms":1795497219489,"completed_at_ms":1795497220145}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T05:13:40.282Z","ordinal":105909,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a20bf9-58ba-70b0-9d08-f02c984f02c9","call_id":"call_c61ee71fa39543b495c30ccc9d8e474a","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(row.dir, \"oversized.bin\"), \"x\");\n    assert.throws(() => integrity.assertTaskSnapshotDigest({\n      dir: row.dir,\n      treeSha256: row.treeSha256,\n      id: row.id,\n      versionedDataset: true,\n    }), /digest mismatch|exceeds/);\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(temp, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"importable runner API passes only evaluator config and keeps credentials private\", async () => {\n  const api = await import(\"./runner_api.mjs\");\n  assert.equal(typeof api.runVersionedEvaluation, \"function\", \"runner API must export versioned evaluation\");\n  const temp = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-runner-api-test-\"));\n  try {\n    const executable = path.join(temp, \"nexus\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(executable, \"#!/bin/sh\\nexit 0\\n\", { mode: 0o700 });\n    const outputDir = path.join(temp, \"output\");\n    let observed;\n    const result = await api.runVersionedEvaluation({\n      config: { apiKey: \"synthetic-test-key\", steps: 3 },\n      nexusExecutable: executable,\n      dataset: datasetRoot,\n      outputDir,\n      split: \"regression\",\n      runs: 2,\n      cwd: temp,\n    }, {\n      run: ({ configPath, ...options }) => {\n        const config = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(configPath, \"utf8\"));\n        observed = {\n          configPath, config, configMode: fs.statSync(configPath).mode & 0o777,\n          credential: fs.readFileSync(config.apiKey.file, \"utf8\"),\n          credentialMode: fs.statSync(config.apiKey.file).mode & 0o777,\n          options,\n        };\n        fs.mkdirSync(options.outputDir, { mode: 0o700 });\n        fs.writeFileSync(path.join(options.outputDir, \"results.jsonl\"), \"{}\\n\");\n      },\n      score: () => ({ taskCount: 1, passRate: 1 }),\n    });\n\n    assert.equal(observed.config.agent, \"nexus\");\n    assert.equal(observed.config.nexusExecutable, executable);\n    assert.deepEqual(observed.config.apiKey, { file: path.join(path.dirname(observed.configPath), \"api-key.env\"), var: \"NEXUS_EVAL_API_KEY\" });\n    assert.equal(observed.configMode, 0o600);\n    assert.equal(observed.credentialMode, 0o600);\n    assert.equal(observed.credential, \"NEXUS_EVAL_API_KEY=REDACTED;\n    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(observed.options.dataset), true);\n    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(observed.configPath), false, \"private runner configuration is removed after completion\");\n    assert.deepEqual(result.score, { taskCount: 1, passRate: 1 });\n    assert.equal(JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(result.scoreFile, \"utf8\")).passRate, 1);\n    assert.equal(fs.statSync(result.scoreFile).mode & 0o777, 0o600);\n    await assert.rejects(api.runVersionedEvaluation({\n      config: {}, nexusExecutable: executable, dataset: datasetRoot, outputDir,\n    }), /output directory must not already exist/);\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(temp, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"dataset loader accepts and decouples code evaluator declarations\", async () => {\n  const loadDataset = requiredLoader();\n  const temp = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-evaluator-decouple-\"));\neval/README.md:78:The committed `eval/datasets/core-v1/` is the first migrated population: one regression self-test and six benchmark\neval/README.md:79:tasks. It can be run through the installed CLI with `nexus eval --dataset eval/datasets/core-v1 --split benchmark`. Held-out qualification corpora remain under their separately approved custody process and are not copied into\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:96:| `node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/eval_dataset.test.ts` (rebased branch; evaluator helper restored to committed mode 0644) | 3 passed, 0 failed | The test initially failed because the shared checkout materialized `eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs` as group-writable (0664), which the evaluator correctly rejects. Correcting only the local file mode to the committed non-writable mode made the provider-stimulus and hidden-validator checks pass; no source or assertion was changed. |\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:99:| `make test` (corrected detached snapshot `2502ae1b`, based on `a5faa878`, with `make build` outputs in the expected paths) | Failed overall, exit 2. Core 53/53, TUI 406/406, scope fixtures, and security lifecycle gates passed. The CLI shard reported 3 failures among 2,493 completed segments and timed out `compaction_continuity.test.ts`. | The run had the compiled CLI and Rust core at expected paths. Failure output includes `eval_dataset.test.ts` (“provider request contains the selected stimulus”); the shard also reported an `ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE` and further assertion failure(s), which were not fully recovered from the sharded output. This is not a clean full-suite qualification; the failures need triage. |\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:108:After rebasing onto PR #739, focused checks passed on the rebased source: context inventory 14/14, provider wire matrix 90/90, agent harness 90/90, slash router 39/39, knowledge controls 3/3, session durable fields 4/4, and persistence protection 27/27. The CLI build passed. On snapshot `48bb93f2` (based on `cebb31ac`, before PR #742), the full turn-semantics suite passed 37/37 and the focused long-step case passed 1/1 after the runtime binaries were placed where the CLI resolves them. After rebasing onto PR #742 at `a57c6c24`, exact-current-source checks passed on `b588d970`: CLI build, context inventory 14/14, knowledge controls 3/3, and provider wire matrix 90/90. At `03b62aaf`, `make build` passed, then `make test` was run with isolated CI-like workspace/runtime fixtures. Rust core passed 53/53, and scope fixtures/security gates passed; the aggregate command failed. Its aggregate test count was not available from the sharded runner output. The isolated `eval_dataset.test.ts` and standalone server-profile eval both fail closed before inference with `compiler exposure could not be checked; refusing qualification`; the gateway saw only the model-list probe, not a chat request. The version-probe test initially rejected the temporary `/tmp` runtime root; a retry used `/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime` and a private 128 MiB tmpfs with the required owner-only mount mode, but the host's bubblewrap could not access the workspace through its `/tmp` parent path. No protected fixture or guard was changed to bypass these checks. The D-04 behavior test exposed an obsolete assertion that expected model-originated `manage_knowledge` to persist durable memory. The test now asserts that this call is rejected and creates no knowledge file; `turn_verdict_evidence.test.ts` passes 26/26. After rebasing onto the latest `origin/release/v1.3.0` at `10942d41`, the focused checks before budget work passed: context inventory 14/14, knowledge controls 3/3, provider wire matrix 90/90, and turn verdict 26/26. The bounded-budget and prompt-provenance implementation passed `npm run build`, `context_inventory.test.ts` 16/16, knowledge controls 3/3, provider wire matrix 90/90, slash router 39/39, persistence protection 27/27, and skill injection 15/15 on exact snapshot `2502ae1b`. The corrected `make test` on snapshot `2502ae1b` passed core 53/53, TUI 406/406, scope fixtures and security gates, but failed overall in the CLI shard: 2,493 completed segments, 3 failures, and a timeout in `compaction_continuity.test.ts`. Focused reruns show the dataset failure came from the local shared-checkout mode of the trusted evaluator helper, and the compaction file completes when the watchdog allows its declared 900-second test timeout. Two of the three CLI failures remain unclassified because the shard output was truncated. The full suite has not been rerun after correcting those local conditions or after rebasing onto `cd755b3e`; repository-wide qualification remains pending.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20bb2-48c0-7db0-bfc5-137d3a66f0eb","create_time":1795497220.2824519}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":47613,"sampled_through_sequence":47610,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
